{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And sometimes [the cloud remained] etc. a number of days.</b> This too tells in Israel's praise, that even when they would not camp for an extended period but only a few days — they would journey when the cloud ascended. And it says <b>at the mouth of HaShem they camped</b>, and the reference of both of them is only to the journey; the verse intends to equate the journeying to the encamping, to say: just as at the mouth of HaShem they camped with willingness and wholehearted resolve to rest from the road, so too with wholehearted willingness they would journey, even though they had rested only a short time." "And I have seen that Targum Yonatan ben Uziel translated ״יָמִים מִסְפָּר״ — שִׁבְעַת יוֹמִין, and according to his words, his memory for a blessing, there is no room for our words to say that the verse comes to praise Israel, for there is enjoyment in resting from the road over the span of seven days. And according to his words, his memory for a blessing, the verse will be expounded in this manner: that it comes to say that both during the interval of encamping and during the interval of journeying, even though they had the desire, they would not do the thing except by virtue of the thing being the decree of the Blessed One, and that is what it says <b>at the mouth of HaShem they camped and at the mouth of HaShem they journeyed</b>:"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:12.608849134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}